cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hexmesh in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "hexmesh: structured all-hex meshes for pipe and duct networks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Karolius
    given-names: Sigve
version: 0.3.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/sigveka/hexmesh"
abstract: >-
  hexmesh builds structured, all-hexahedral, conformal meshes of pipe and
  duct networks with GMSH, including tees, wyes and duct taps, with fluid,
  wall and insulation as separate regions for conjugate heat transfer.
  It writes OpenFOAM cases, predicts cell counts exactly before meshing,
  and keeps mesh connectivity fixed across parameter studies.
keywords:
  - CFD
  - mesh generation
  - hexahedral mesh
  - structured mesh
  - pipe networks
  - OpenFOAM
  - gmsh
  - conjugate heat transfer
